1
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:35,199
好的，上次我们研究了 R^n 的刚体运动群， 即由 R^n 到 R^n 保持两点 v 到 w 之间距离函数 d 的运动 M 所构成的群 G，
Okay, so last time we were studying the group of motions of R^n,   the group G of motions M from R^n to R^n which preserve the distance function d from v to w,

2
00:00:35,199 --> 00:00:48,743
该距离就是绝对值（范数）|v - w|；它是所有保持两点间距离的 R^n 到 R^n 的集合论映射，所以这应当等于 d(M(v), M(w))。
which is absolute value |v - w|, so it's all set-theoretic maps from R^n to R^n which preserve the distance between the two points, so this should be equal to d of M(v), M(w).

3
00:00:48,743 --> 00:01:17,120
我们还观察到它包含一个同构于加法群 R^n 本身的平移子群， 也就是如果你在 R^n 中有一个向量 b，你把任意向量 v 映射到 v + b，这就是对向量进行平移。
And we observed that there's a subgroup of this isomorphic to R^n itself under addition of translations,   and those are things if you have a vector b in R^n and you just take an arbitrary vector v to v + b, so that translates vectors.

4
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:27,642
这显然保持距离，因为两点间的距离只取决于距离——即两个向量之差，而平移后两向量之差保持不变。
And that clearly preserves the distance because the distance only depends on the distance—the difference between two vectors, so the difference is the same if you translate.

5
00:01:27,642 --> 00:01:47,950
现在我断言，G 中的任意元素都可以唯一地写成一个平移（该子群中的元素），乘以一个来自我记作 G_0 的子群中的元素，其中 G_0 是保持原点不动的运动。
Now I claim that any element in G can be written uniquely as a translation, an element in this subgroup, times an element in the subgroup I'll call G_0, where these are the motions that preserve the origin.

6
00:01:52,320 --> 00:02:16,109
这很显然，因为如果我有一个任意变换，它把原点映到某个位置，即 M(0) 等于某个向量 b。
And that's clear, because if I have an arbitrary transformation, then it takes the origin somewhere, i.e., M of 0 is equal to some b.

7
00:02:16,109 --> 00:02:44,152
那么如果我把 M 与平移复合——看看，对，M 与平移复合，不妨把这个平移记作 T_b 或别的，T_{-b}(M(0)) 现在就等于 0 了，所以这是 G_0 中的一个元素，并且它是一个平移乘以 M。
So if I just compose M with the translation—let's see, yeah, M composed with the translation, let's call this translation T_b or something, T_{-b} of M of 0 is now equal to 0, so this is an element in G_0, and it's a translation times M.

8
00:02:44,152 --> 00:02:54,051
因此两边乘以 T_b^{-1}，我就把任意元素 M 写成了一个平移乘上 G_0 中的某个元素。并且这两个群没有非平凡交集，因为除恒等映射外没有平移能保原点。
So multiplying by T_b inverse, I get M as—get the arbitrary element as a translation times something in G_0. And these two groups have no intersection because no translation preserves 0.

9
00:02:54,051 --> 00:02:56,558
所以每个元素都唯一地写成平移乘以保持 0 不动的变换。
So everything is uniquely written as a translation times something fixing 0.

10
00:02:56,558 --> 00:03:08,046
上次我还断言 G_0同构于 O(n)，即正交变换群。
And the last time I claimed was that G_0 was isomorphic to O(n), the group of orthogonal transformations.

11
00:03:08,046 --> 00:03:23,789
这显然包含在 G_0 中，因为正交变换是线性映射所以保持 0；而且它们保持内积，从而保持距离，对吧，因为距离正是 v - w 与自身内积的平方根。
Clearly this is contained in G_0, because these are linear maps so they preserve 0; they preserve the inner product so they preserve the distance, right, because this is just the inner product of v - w with v - w, the square root of it.

12
00:03:23,789 --> 00:03:33,940
所以任何保持内积的变换都保持距离，因而这必然包含在 G_0 中。关键在于证明它就是整个 G_0。
So anything that preserves the inner product preserves the distance, and so this is certainly contained in G_0. And the trick is to show it's all of G_0.

13
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:39,516
并且上次的关键技巧是：如果它保持距离，它也保持内积；但我们还不知道它是线性的。
And the trick last time I showed that if it preserved the distance it also preserves the inner product, but we don't know that it's linear.

14
00:03:39,516 --> 00:03:59,254
我必须向大家证明它是线性的，所以我现在用以下方式证明这是一个同构。取 G_0 中的一个元素 M，断言是 <M(v), M(w)> = <v, w>。这就是我们上次证明的内容：它保持内积，原因在于(w) 等于 <v, w>。
I have to prove to you that it's linear, so I'm now going to prove that this is an isomorphism in the following way. Take an element in G_0, so M in G_0. The claim is that <M(v), M(w)> is equal to <v, w>. This is what we proved last time, that it preserves the inner product. And the reason is (w) is equal to <v, w>.

15
00:03:59,254 --> 00:04:17,724
这就是我们上次证明的内容：它保持内积，原因在于因为你有公式：d(v, w)^2 等于 d(v, 0)^2 + d(w, 0)^2 减去两倍的内积。
This is what we proved last time, that it preserves the inner product, and the reason is because you have the formula that d(v, w)^2 is equal to d(v, 0)^2 + d(w, 0)^2 minus two times the inner product.

16
00:04:17,724 --> 00:04:28,494
如果你把这个展开，会得到 <v, v> + <w, w> - 2<v, w>，其中 <v, v> 是 v 到 0 的距离平方，加 <w, w>即 w 到 0 的距离平方。
If you expand this out, you get <v, v> + <w, w> - 2<v, w>, and <v, v> is the distance from v to 0 squared, plus <w, w> which is the distance from w to 0 squared.

17
00:04:28,494 --> 00:04:42,760
因此如果你有一个保持原点的运动群，它保持两点之间的距离；由于它保持原点，它就保持向量到原点的距离；它保持 w 到原点的距离，所以它必须保持这个内积。
So if you have a group of motions that preserves the origin, it preserves the distance between two points; since it preserves the origin, it preserves the distance of a vector from the origin; it preserves the distance of w from the origin, so it has to preserve this inner product.

18
00:04:42,760 --> 00:05:04,565
因此该子群中的任何元素都保持内积。现在考虑它对标准正交基的作用：设 e_1 到 e_n 为R^n 的标准基。我们拿到粉笔了吗？在那儿呢，好的。
So anything in this subgroup preserves the inner product. Now consider what it does to an orthonormal basis: let e_1 through e_n be the standard basis of R^n. Did we ever get chalk? There it is, okay.

19
00:05:04,565 --> 00:05:18,486
现在这组基具有如下性质：如果你取这些基向量与自身的内积得到 1，取基向量与另一个不同基向量的内积得到 0。
Now this has the property that if you take the inner products of the basis vectors with themselves you get 1, and you take the inner product of the basis vectors with another basis vector you get 0.

20
00:05:18,486 --> 00:05:51,344
那么 M(e_1), M(e_2), ..., M(e_n)是另一组标准正交基，对吧，因为 G_0 中的这个变换 M 保持内积，所以这些向量的长度都是 1，并且它们彼此正交。
Then M(e_1), M(e_2), ..., M(e_n) is another orthonormal basis, right, because this transformation M, which is in G_0, preserves the inner product, and therefore the lengths of these vectors are 1 and they are orthogonal to each other.

21
00:05:51,344 --> 00:06:21,735
现在考虑以下正交变换： 设 A 为 O(n) 中的元素， 其列向量为 M(e_1), M(e_2), ..., M(e_n)。这是一个正交变换，因为我们知道这些列向量是标准正交的。
Now consider the following orthogonal transformation:   let A be the element in O(n)   with column vectors M(e_1), M(e_2), ..., M(e_n). That's an orthogonal transformation, because these column vectors are, we know, orthonormal.

22
00:06:21,735 --> 00:06:32,070
而列向量标准正交的事实，恰好说明 A^T A 是单位矩阵，这就是正交变换的定义。
And the fact that the column vectors are orthonormal is exactly the statement that A^T A is the identity matrix, and that's what it means to be an orthogonal transformation.

23
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:46,249
所以一旦我有一组标准正交基，并构造把这组基映到那组基的变换，那就是一个正交变换。
So once I have a collection of orthonormal—an orthonormal basis, and I make the transformation that takes this basis to this basis, that's an orthogonal transformation.

24
00:06:46,249 --> 00:06:55,269
当然，我正在证明 G_0 中的任意元素都由某个正交变换给出。
Sure, I'm showing that any element in G_0 is given by an orthogonal transformation.

25
00:06:55,269 --> 00:07:16,355
所以我从 G_0 中的一个元素出发，证明了它保持内积，我把该元素作用在标准基上，得到一组新的标准正交基，现在我写出一个把原基映到这组新基的矩阵——那是一个正交变换。
So I started with an element in G_0, I proved that it preserves the inner product, I apply that element to my standard basis, I get a new orthonormal basis, and now I write down a matrix that takes this basis to this basis—that's an orthogonal transformation.

26
00:07:17,105 --> 00:07:23,865
现在的断言是：作为 R^n 上的变换，M 等于 A。
The claim is M is equal to A as a transformation of R^n.

27
00:07:23,865 --> 00:07:37,831
也就是说——我所做的只是构造了正交群中的一个元素，它对这 n 个不同的向量具有与 M 相同的效果；现在我要证明它对每一个向量都具有与 M 相同的效果。
Namely, this—all I've done is constructed an element in the orthogonal group that does the same thing as M to these n different vectors, and now I'm going to show it does the same thing as M to every vector.

28
00:07:37,831 --> 00:07:48,056
好的，这就是我要证明的。 M(v) 是什么？
Okay, that's what I'm going to try to prove.   What is M(v)?

29
00:07:48,056 --> 00:08:12,642
M(v) 是某个向量，不妨称它为 w，有 n 个坐标 (w_1, ..., w_n)，而 v 是向量 (v_1, ..., v_n)。好的，M(v) 的坐标是什么？
Well, M(v) is some vector that looks like—let's call it, sorry, w, has n coordinates (w_1, ..., w_n), and v is the vector (v_1, ..., v_n). Okay, what are the coordinates of M(v)?

30
00:08:12,642 --> 00:08:24,030
计算M(v) 坐标的方法是：w_i 是 M(v) 与标准基向量 e_i 的内积。
Well, the way you calculate the coordinates of M(v) is that w_i is the inner product of M(v) with the standard basis vector e_i.

31
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:49,879
好的，现在我要换一种略有不同的方式——先把这里擦掉一下，但本质一样。为了证明 M 等于 A，考虑运动 M与 A^{-1} 的复合。
Okay, now I'm going to do it slightly differently—erase this for a second, but same thing. To show that M is equal to A, consider the motion M composed with A inverse.

32
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:53,302
把这个运动记作 M'。
Call that motion M'.

33
00:08:53,302 --> 00:09:08,569
这是空间的一个刚体运动，它保持距离，因为原假设 M 保持距离；它属于 G_0，而 A 是正交变换、我们已知它保持距离，所以这个复合也保持距离。
That's a motion of space, preserves distance because M was assumed to preserve distance, wherever it was; it's in G_0, and A is an orthogonal transformation which we know preserves distance, so this thing preserves distance.

34
00:09:08,569 --> 00:09:19,338
它属于 G_0，并且具有对所有 i 都有 M'(e_i) = e_i 的性质。
This is in G_0, and it has the property that M'(e_i) is equal to e_i for all i.

35
00:09:19,338 --> 00:09:39,408
我想证明对 R^n 中的所有 v，都有 M'(v) = v，即作为变换，A 在 R^n 上等于 M。
And I want to show M'(v) is equal to v for all v in R^n, i.e., A is equal to M on R^n as a transformation.

36
00:09:39,408 --> 00:09:55,080
所以我知道我构造了一个正交矩阵，使得当我把它的逆复合到原变换上时，我得到了一个保持标准正交基的每个元素不动的变换。我想证明它保持每一个向量不动，这就是诀窍所在。
So I know I've constructed an orthogonal matrix such that when I multiply by its inverse on my transformation, I have a transformation that fixes every element of my orthonormal basis. I want to show it fixes every vector, that's the trick.

37
00:09:55,080 --> 00:10:15,038
那么 M'(v) 的坐标是什么？M'(v) 的第 i 个坐标是 M'(v)与第 i 个基向量的内积。
Well, what are the coordinates of M'(v)? The i-th coordinate of M'(v) is the inner product of M'(v) with the i-th basis vector.

38
00:10:15,038 --> 00:10:23,289
现在由于 M'(e_i) = e_i，这等价于 M'(v)与 M'(e_i) 的内积。
Now since M'(e_i) is e_i, this is the same thing as the inner product of M'(v) with M'(e_i).

39
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:36,405
又因为 M' 是保持原点不动的运动，这与 v与 e_i 的内积相同，而这正是 v 的第 i 个坐标！
And since M' is a motion that fixes the origin, this is the same as the inner product of v with e_i, and this is the i-th coordinate of v!

40
00:10:36,405 --> 00:11:04,447
因此 M'(v) 的第 i 个坐标与 v 的第 i 个坐标完全相同，这意味着 M' 保持 v 不动。对，我刚才写到哪里了——就是这里。
So the i-th coordinate of M'(v) is the same as the i-th coordinate of v, which means that M' fixes v. Yeah, where I went— this one here.

41
00:11:04,447 --> 00:11:09,820
我有一个向量 v，我想证明它在 M' 下固定不变。
So I have a vector v, I'm trying to prove it's fixed by M'.

42
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:22,396
所以只需证明M'(v) 的每个分量都与 v 的分量相同。第 i 个分量就是这个。现在因为 M' 保持 e_i 不动，我可以把它替换成这个。
So it suffices to prove that every component of M'(v) is the same as the component of v. So here's the i-th component, it is this. Now since M' fixes e_i, I can replace it by this.

43
00:11:22,396 --> 00:11:35,515
现在利用 M' 是保持原点的刚体运动这一事实，因此它保持内积：结果就是这个，即 v_i，也就是 v 的第 i 个坐标。这证明了 M'(v) = v。
Now I use the fact that M' is a motion which preserves the origin, so it preserves the inner product: it's this, which is v_i, which is the i-th coordinate of v. So that shows that M'(v) is equal to v.

44
00:11:35,515 --> 00:11:48,672
所以让我们来回顾这有多么巧妙：我们给定一个保持原点不动的任意刚体运动；我们通过一个对标准正交基具有相同作用的矩阵构造出一个正交变换，
So let's go over how clever this is: we are given an arbitrary motion that fixes the origin; we construct an orthogonal transformation by a matrix that has the same effect on an orthonormal basis,

45
00:11:48,672 --> 00:12:06,694
但我们一开始不知道它对每个向量都具有相同作用；接着我们通过利用与正交基的内积还原向量坐标，证明了它对每个向量都有相同作用。非常巧妙的证明！
but we don't know it has the same effect on every vector; and then we show it has the same effect on every vector by recovering the coordinates of the vector via the inner product with our orthogonal basis. Very clever proof!

46
00:12:06,694 --> 00:12:12,276
因此我们现在对刚体运动群有了完整的描述。刚体运动群现在呈现出这样的形态。
So we now have a complete description of the group of motions. The group of motions now looks like this.

47
00:12:12,276 --> 00:12:25,130
让我们把群乘法也写下来，因为既然我们知道了其中的元素——G_0 中的元素现在已经与正交变换建立了双射对应。对每个 M 我们都关联了一个矩阵 A，属于 O(n)。
And let's write down what the product is too, because now that we know the elements in it—the elements in G_0 we've now identified bijectively with the orthogonal transformations. For every M we associated a matrix A, so this is O(n).

48
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:44,120
元素 M 作用在 v 上——如果我们有这里的有序对 (b, A)，一个平移和一个正交矩阵 A。M 对 v 的作用是把它映到 A(v)，即正交变换，再加上 b。
An element M of v—where if we have the pair here, we have (b, A), a translation and an orthogonal matrix A. What M does to v is it takes it to A(v), the orthogonal transformation, plus b.

49
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:52,889
这是在 n 维空间中得到保持距离的变换的唯一方式，比正交群略微更具一般性。
That's the only way you can get a transformation of n-dimensional space that preserves the distance, slightly more general than the orthogonal group.

50
00:12:52,889 --> 00:13:02,420
那么如果我们取 (b, A) 与 (b', A') 的乘积会怎样？在这个群中乘积是什么样子？
And what happens if we take the product of (b, A) with (b', A')? What does that product look like in this group?

51
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:15,262
如果我们把它作用于向量 v，这就是 (b, A) 作用于向量 A'(v) + b'，因为这正是后者对向量 v 所做的。
Well, if we apply it to a vector v, this is (b, A) applied to the vector A'(v) + b', because that's what this does to the vector v.

52
00:13:15,262 --> 00:13:33,779
现在我们算算它的效果：首先我们把正交变换作用在这个向量上，变成 A(A'(v) + b')。这是一个新向量：我们对其施加正交变换，然后平移 b。
And now let's figure out what this does: first we apply the orthogonal transformation to this vector, that becomes A(A'(v) + b'). This is a new vector: we apply the orthogonal transformation to it, and then we translate by b.

53
00:13:33,779 --> 00:13:49,030
如果合并同类项，我们发现正交群中的乘积 A A'作用在 v 上，加上向量 A(b') + b 的平移。
And if we gather up terms, we find the product of A A' as an element in the orthogonal group applied to v, plus translation by the vector A(b') + b.

54
00:13:49,030 --> 00:14:03,919
因此如果我想在群中写出这个元素乘以那个元素的乘法法则，它就等于元素 (b + A(b'), A A')。
And so if I wanted to write down the product law of this times this in the group, it would equal the element (b + A(b'), A A').

55
00:14:03,919 --> 00:14:17,474
这就是这些元素在运动群中的乘法。它不是直积群——如果是直积群，就会得到 (b + b', A A')。
That's what this product of these elements is in this group of motions. It's not a direct product group—if it were a direct product group, I'd have (b + b', A A').

56
00:14:17,474 --> 00:14:21,782
它不完全是积群，因此这些元素彼此并不对易。
It's not quite a product group, so these things don't commute with each other.

57
00:14:21,782 --> 00:14:36,780
但请注意，我的确得到了一个到正交群的同态，也就是说，如果我现在考虑从刚体运动出发、只保留其正交变换的映射——
But note that I do get a homomorphism to the orthogonal group, namely, if I now consider the map that takes me from a motion and it just remembers the orthogonal transformation—

58
00:14:36,780 --> 00:15:07,773
把二元对 (b, A) 映为正交变换 A，这是一个满群同态，其核为 R^n。即核是由形如 (b, I) 的所有元素构成的，其中 I 为单位矩阵。
that takes a pair (b, A) to just the orthogonal transformation A, this is a surjective group homomorphism with kernel R^n. Namely, the kernel is the elements—all of the things of the form (b, I), the identity matrix.

59
00:15:07,773 --> 00:15:16,280
因为当我在群里取两个元素的乘积并只保留其正交分量时，它就是这两个矩阵的乘积，所以那一部分是同态。
Because when I take the product of two elements here and I just remember their orthogonal component, it's the product of the two matrices, so that part is a homomorphism.

60
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:27,856
而该同态的核是所有映到单位矩阵的变换，它们恰好就是平移。
And the kernel of that homomorphism is all the transformations that go to the identity matrix here, so those are just the translations.

61
00:15:27,856 --> 00:15:35,391
它们具有作用在 v 上只得到 v + b 的性质；这就是我们所说的 T_b。
These have the property that when you act on v, you just get v + b; this is what we call T_b.

62
00:15:35,391 --> 00:16:01,053
因此这个群由两个群、两个子群拼合而成：一个是正规子群（平移子群是正规子群）；而另一个子群 O(n)通过这个同态同构于商群。
So the group is put together out of two groups, two subgroups: one is a normal subgroup, so this is a normal subgroup; and the other subgroup O(n) is isomorphic to the quotient group via this homomorphism.

63
00:16:01,053 --> 00:16:10,604
现在，本讲剩下的时间将集中讨论 n = 2 的情形，因为这是个极其丰富的情形。
So now the rest of the lecture is going to be on the situation when n is equal to 2, because that's an incredibly rich situation.

64
00:16:10,604 --> 00:16:15,437
接下来的两讲我们将专门研究平面的刚体运动以及它们保持什么图形。
We're going to spend the next two lectures just looking at motions of the plane and what figures they preserve.

65
00:16:15,437 --> 00:16:26,941
这是自古代发展起来的对称群的完整理论，并且仅仅在 n = 2 时，它就已经是一个迷人而异常丰富的群了。
This is the whole theory that was developed in ancient times of symmetry groups, and already for n = 2 it's a fascinating group, an incredibly rich group.

66
00:16:26,941 --> 00:16:40,658
我们在之前的内容中已经推导了 O(2) 中的元素是什么样子。对于 n = 2，我们讨论的是群 G，即 R^2 与 O(2) 的半直积。
So what we did previously was we worked out what elements in O(2) look like. So for n = 2 we're talking about the group G which is R^2 semidirect O(2).

67
00:16:40,658 --> 00:17:18,403
如果平移是平凡的，O(2) 就是 G_0；我们看到它包含一个子群 SO(2)（即绕原点的旋转），此外还有一个非平凡陪集（我记作 r_L），其中的元素阶数全为 2，它们是关于某条直线的反射，一条过原点的直线。
So if the translation is trivial, O(2) is G_0, and we saw that that contained a subgroup SO(2) which was the rotations around the origin, and then there was a non-trivial coset of that which I'll call r_L, where the elements in this non-trivial coset all had order 2, and they were reflections across a line, a line through the origin.

68
00:17:18,403 --> 00:17:35,698
如果有一条过原点的直线，你取其垂直向量，就会得到在直线上特征值为 +1、而在法线上是特征值 -1 的特征空间的变换，使得一般向量正是关于这条直线反射。
So that if one had a line that was through the origin, you took the perpendicular vector, you got a transformation that was +1 on this line, and where this was an eigenspace with eigenvalue -1, so that the general vector was just reflected across this line.

69
00:17:35,698 --> 00:17:47,630
所以如果你有一个向量v，它被映到向量——在这里，同样的距离，这是 v，这是 r_L(v)，其中L 是直线。
So if you had a vector v, it was taken to the vector—well, over here, the same distance here, this would be v, this would be r_L(v), where this was the line L.

70
00:17:47,630 --> 00:18:02,070
因此对过原点的每条直线，我们都有一个行列式为 -1 的正交变换，其特征值为 +1 和 -1，在正交直线上是 -1；它对一般向量的效果就是关于该直线作反射。
So for every line through the origin, we had an orthogonal transformation of determinant -1, where the eigenvalues are +1 and -1, -1 on the orthogonal line; and the effect on a general vector is to reflect it across that line.

71
00:18:02,070 --> 00:18:14,260
这就是那个非平凡陪集，而另一部分则是绕原点的旋转，这是我们上次讲过的内容。
And that was the non-trivial coset, where these were the rotations around the origin, and that we did last time.

72
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:30,686
上次我们还有一件事没做，如果真想透彻理解这个群就必须做这件事：SO(2) 是一个交换群，复合旋转只需将角度相加，乘法顺序不会产生任何影响。
Now we didn't do one thing last time which we have to do if we really want to understand this group, namely, this is a commutative group: if you compose rotations, you just add the angles; it doesn't make any difference in what order you multiply.

73
00:18:30,686 --> 00:18:46,350
但我们想看看用反射去共轭一个旋转会发生什么。那么 r_L 与旋转rho_theta 复合再乘 r_L^{-1} 的公式是什么？
But we want to see what happens when we conjugate a rotation by a reflection. So what is the formula for r_L of the rotation through theta composed with r_L inverse?

74
00:18:46,350 --> 00:18:57,280
因为这将给出该群中乘法法则的结构。我们知道旋转之间如何相乘，如果包含反射陪集中的元素，我们也必须知道如何相乘，对吧？
Because that will give us the structure of the multiplication law in this group. We know how to multiply things in here, we have to know how to multiply things if we have something in here too, okay?

75
00:18:57,280 --> 00:19:03,102
这其实非常容易算出来。顺便说一句，r_L^{-1} 是什么？就是 r_L！
Now this turns out to be very simple to work out. By the way, r_L inverse is what? r_L!

76
00:19:03,102 --> 00:19:19,643
因为你想想这个反射，连做两次就回到了恒等变换。所以这也可以写成 r_L o rho_theta o r_L。
Because if you think about this reflection, if you do it twice, you get back to the identity. So this can also be written as r_L composed with rotation by theta composed with r_L.

77
00:19:19,643 --> 00:19:30,916
现在我断言，根本不用深思——虽然我们待会儿要仔细推导——这就是绕某个其他角度 theta' 的旋转。
Now I claim, without doing any thought at all—but we're going to have to do some thought in a moment—that this is the rotation through some other angle theta prime.

78
00:19:30,916 --> 00:19:32,543
而我们要做的是算出 theta' 是多少。
And what we have to do is figure out what theta prime is.

79
00:19:32,543 --> 00:19:44,600
我现在凭什么知道无论该变换在 O(2) 中是什么，它都必须是绕某个角度的旋转呢？
Now how do I know that whatever this transformation is in O(2), it has to be a rotation through an angle theta prime?

80
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:52,131
对，它显然保原点——所有这些变换都保原点！
Yeah, it certainly fixes—all these things fix the origin!

81
00:19:52,131 --> 00:20:04,750
关键在于它的行列式为 1，因为反射的行列式为 -1，旋转的行列式为 1，另一个反射行列式为 -1，所以复合的行列式为 1！它是一个旋转；我们只需确定旋转角。
And the point is that this thing has determinant 1, because this has determinant -1, this has determinant 1, and this has determinant -1, so the composition has determinant 1! It's a rotation; all we have to do is figure out the angle.

82
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:12,222
现在为了确定角度，我们只需追踪该变换下的一个点，对吧？
Now to figure out the angle, all we've got to do is follow one point under this transformation, right?

83
00:20:12,222 --> 00:20:29,102
所以我们要这么做：这是直线 L，我们将追踪 L 上一个点的行为，看它被旋转到了哪里。一旦搞清楚这一点，我就知道所有点被转到了哪里。
So here's what we're going to do: here's our line L, we're going to follow the behavior of a point on L and see where it gets rotated. And once we do that, I know where everything gets rotated.

84
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:35,969
好的，如果我把这个变换作用于 L 上的一个点 P 会怎样？第一步做了什么？什么也没做！
Okay, what happens if I apply this transformation to a point on L? What does the first part of it do? It does nothing!

85
00:20:35,969 --> 00:20:44,020
它保持 L 固定：这条线在反射下固定不动，所以 P 留在原地。所以 r_L(P) = P。
It fixes L: this line is fixed by the reflection, so P stays where it is. So this is equal to r_L(P), and it's r_L(P), sorry.

86
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:57,954
接着下一步是我把它旋转角度 theta，它就变到了 (rho_theta o r_L)(P)。
And then the next thing I do is I rotate it through an angle of theta, and it goes over to rho_theta composed with r_L of P.

87
00:20:57,954 --> 00:21:16,060
最后一步是关于直线 L 进行反射。这是最终的点：(r_L o rho_theta o r_L)(P)。
And then the final thing I have to do is the reflection across the line L. Here's the final point: r_L of rho_theta composed with r_L of P.

88
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:34,104
它把点映到了 L 的另一侧。这里的夹角是多少？正好是 -theta！所以我所做的就是取了点 P 并将其旋转了 -theta。这就是公式！
It takes it to the other side of L. What's this angle here? -theta, exactly! So what I've done is I've taken P and I've rotated it by -theta. So that's the formula!

89
00:21:34,104 --> 00:21:43,144
顺便说一句，这个旋转与 rho_theta 的逆变换相同，因为如果你想求旋转 theta 的逆，只需往回转 -theta。
And this rotation, by the way, is the same thing as rotation of theta inverse, because if you wanted to invert the rotation of theta, you rotate back by -theta.

90
00:21:43,144 --> 00:21:58,155
所以在特别地，这是一个非常酷的群：SO(2) 是一个交换群，并且该陪集中的任何元素（因为该陪集中的任何元素都是某个 r_L）都满足：
So in particular, this is a very cool group: this is a commutative group, and anything in this coset—because anything in this coset is some r_L—has the fact that when you conjugate,

91
00:21:58,155 --> 00:22:15,910
当你进行共轭时（SO(2) 是正规子群），如果你取该子群 H 中的任意元素并用子群外的元素对其共轭，你就会得到这个恒等式。
this is a normal subgroup, and if you have anything in this group H and you conjugate it by anything outside it, you get this identity.

92
00:22:15,910 --> 00:22:22,112
所以它不是交换群，因为 r 与 H 不对易，但它把 H 中的任意元素 h 变成 h^{-1}。
So it's not a commutative group because r doesn't commute with H, but it takes h to h inverse for any element in H.

93
00:22:22,112 --> 00:22:35,560
在这里H 属于 SO(2)，r 属于非平凡陪集。两个不同陪集中的元素相乘时，就会产生求逆关系。
And here H is in SO(2), and r is in the non-trivial coset. Anything in one coset and you try to commute with anything in the other, you get the inverse.

94
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:41,768
这就是这个群里的乘法法则！很好，非常有趣。
So that's the multiplication law in this group! Good, very interesting.

95
00:22:41,768 --> 00:22:52,719
而我们推导它所做的一切，不过是知道它是一个旋转，我们只需弄清楚它对某一个点做了什么。我们很明智地选择了直线上的点，这样第一个变换对它什么也没改变。
And all we did to figure that out was we knew it was a rotation; all we had to figure out was what it did to one point. We conveniently chose the point on the line, so the first transformation did nothing to it.

96
00:22:52,719 --> 00:23:00,893
好的，这些就是对群 O(2)（即我们所说的 G_0）中元素的描述。
Okay, those are our descriptions of elements in the group O(2), which is what we call G_0.

97
00:23:00,893 --> 00:23:13,508
但真正令人惊奇的是，你可以对 G 中的所有元素都给出简单的描述！这是一个重要定理：G 中的任意元素都具有简明的几何描述。
But what's amazing is that you get simple descriptions of all elements in G! So that's a big theorem, that any element in G has a simple geometric description.

98
00:23:13,508 --> 00:23:16,940
共有四种基本类型。
There are four basic types.

99
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:42,327
第一种：还记得我们有一个从 G 到 O(2) 的映射，就是上面的这个同态；而在 O(2) 上我们有另一个同态——行列式，把矩阵映为 +1 或 -1。
One: well, remember we have a map from G to O(2), this homomorphism up here; and on O(2) we have another homomorphism, the determinant, that takes us to +1 or -1.

100
00:23:42,327 --> 00:23:51,784
因此我们在 G 中有一个子群，由那些先映到 O(2) 然后取行列式等于 +1 的元素组成。
So we have a subgroup of G consisting of the elements when you first map them to O(2) and then you take the determinant, they are +1.

101
00:23:51,784 --> 00:23:54,491
这些被称为 G 中的保定向元素。
Those are called the orientation-preserving elements in G.

102
00:23:54,491 --> 00:24:10,545
所以我们要有那些 det(g)（如果允许我这么称呼的话）等于 +1 的保定向元素；然后有那些 det(g) = -1 的反定向元素。
So we're going to have those whose determinant of g—if you allow me to say this—is +1, orientation-preserving; and then you have the elements whose determinant of g is -1, orientation-reversing.

103
00:24:10,545 --> 00:24:27,788
现在我们知道任何行列式为 +1 的元素都具有平移 T_b 与旋转 rho_theta 复合的形式。但那是很复杂的描述，因为我们并不真正清楚它对一个点做了什么。
Now we know that any element which is of determinant +1 has the form translation by b composed with rotation theta. But that's a complicated description, because we don't really know what that does to a point.

104
00:24:27,788 --> 00:24:31,350
它说的是：先旋转 theta 再平移 b，这到底意味着什么？
It says, you know, first you rotate it by theta and translate by b: what does that really mean?

105
00:24:31,350 --> 00:24:46,800
而在反定向这边我们知道，每个元素都具有平移 T_b 复合旋转 rho_theta 再复合关于直线 L 的反射的形式，因为非平凡陪集由平移以及这里的元素构成。
And here we know that everything has the form translation by b composed with rotation by theta composed with reflection across a line L, because the non-trivial coset is, you know, translations and elements in here.

106
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:52,756
但这在几何上不太直观，因为我们看不出它们在做什么。
But that's not very useful because geometrically we don't see what these are doing.

107
00:24:52,756 --> 00:25:10,240
其实它们属于四种几何类型之一：保定向给出了两种类型。第一种是纯平移，形式就是 T_b：你把每个点平移相同的向量，对吧？
It's one of four geometric types: so this gives two types. One are just pure translations, and those are just of the form T_b: there you just take every point and translate, right?

108
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:13,820
这是最简单的情形，旋转是平凡的。
Here that's the simplest case of this, where the rotation is trivial.

109
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:31,889
第二种——这些平移不固定任何点，或者固定所有点（当 b = 0 时，即恒等变换）：恒等变换固定 R^2 中的每个点，但一般平移不固定任何点。
And the second is—so these translations fix no points, or all points if b is equal to 0, if it's the identity element: it fixes every point in R^2, but the general translation fixes nothing.

110
00:25:31,889 --> 00:25:49,156
接着是这种形式中固定单个点的元素，它们由绕 P 的旋转组成。
And then there are the elements of this form that fix a single point, and consist of rotations around P.

111
00:25:49,156 --> 00:26:02,526
从当前的代数表示完全看不出这一点，但我们将看到形如这类的元素要么是平移（不固定任何点），要么固定单个点并绕其旋转。
That's not obvious from this presentation at all, but we're going to see that anything of this form either is a translation (fixes nothing), or fixes a single point and rotates points around that.

112
00:26:02,526 --> 00:26:33,243
而反定向形式的元素要么是所谓的反射——即 b = 0 的情形，形式为关于直线 L' 的反射 r_{L'}；要么是所谓的滑动反射（滑移反射），即先关于直线作反射，然后与平行于该直线的向量平移复合。
Anything of this form is either what's called a reflection—that's where b is equal to 0, so that's of the form reflection r_{L'} across a line—or what's called a glide reflection, where you reflect across the line and then you compose that with translation by a vector parallel to the line.

113
00:26:33,243 --> 00:26:48,670
反射具有固定直线 L 上每个点的性质，因为反射保持直线 L 上的所有点不动；而滑动反射不逐点固定直线 L 上的向量，
So this has the property of fixing everything on the line L, because the reflection fixes everything on the line L; and this has the property that it doesn't fix every vector on the line L,

114
00:26:48,670 --> 00:27:07,127
但它把直线 L 作为整体集合保持不变（非逐点固定），因为反射固定了直线上的所有向量，然后你沿着该直线平行平移。
but it fixes the line L not pointwise, because this fixes all the vectors on the line and then you're translating by something parallel along the line.

115
00:27:07,127 --> 00:27:14,151
所以第一步把点保持在直线上，然后你只需沿平行于 L 的向量平移。
So the first thing takes your point here and then you just translate by a vector that's running parallel to L.

116
00:27:14,151 --> 00:27:27,000
因此这个运动群 G 中的变换令人惊叹之处在于它们恰好分为四类：那些什么都不固定的变换（既不固定点也不固定线）；固定单个点的变换；
So the amazing thing about these transformations in this motion group G is they come in four types: the things that fix nothing, neither points nor lines; the things that fix a single point;

117
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:38,888
逐点固定直线上所有点的变换——这些是R^2 中的反射；以及把直线作为一个集合保持不变的变换——这些是滑动反射。就这四种！
the things that fix points on a line pointwise—those are the reflections in R^2; and the things that fix a line as a set—those are the glide reflections. And that's it!

118
00:27:38,888 --> 00:28:00,804
对每个元素，你要么不能关联任何固定对象（它只是一个向量、纯平移），要么可以给它关联一个点，要么关联一条直线，或者给它关联一条直线和一个滑动向量。我现在要向大家证明第一部分，第二部分留给大家看书自学。
Every element you can either associate to it nothing (it's just a vector, a translation), or you can associate to it a point, or you can associate to it a line, or you can—or you can associate to it a line and a glide vector. So I'm going to prove to you this part, and I'll leave this part for you to look at in the book.

119
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:03,263
同样，关键技巧是找到那条直线、找到那个点。
Again, the trick is finding the line, finding the point.

120
00:28:03,263 --> 00:28:24,320
所以让我们看看能不能——看看我们能否完成前一半：把行列式为 1 的陪集中的每个元素分解为平移，或者绕某个未指定点的旋转。好的，如果 theta = 0，
So let's see if we can—let's see if we can do the first half of this: break up everything in this determinant 1 coset to either a translation or a rotation around some unspecified point.

121
00:28:24,320 --> 00:28:42,497
这是 theta = 0 的情形，而那是 theta != 0 的情形。好，如果 theta != 0 且 b != 0，我将向大家展示不动点 P 在哪里。
Okay, so if theta is equal to 0, this is where theta is equal to 0, and this is where theta is not equal to 0, all right.

122
00:28:42,497 --> 00:29:12,872
如果 b等于 0，那么不动点 P 就是原点 0，我们就回到了 G_0 中，也就是我们已经掌握的群。 因此假设 b 也不为 0：不动点在哪里呢？
So I'm going to show you where the fixed point P is if theta is not equal to 0 and b is not equal to 0. If b is equal to 0, then P is just the point 0, and we are in G_0, and in the group that we already know.   So assume b is also not equal to 0:

123
00:29:12,872 --> 00:29:31,984
我画个简图来说明如何找到这个变换的不动点：首先旋转 theta，然后平移 b，其中 theta 是非零角度，b 是非零向量。
where is the fixed point? So I'll draw you a little picture of how you find the fixed point for this transformation: first you rotate by theta and then you translate by b, and theta is a nonzero angle and b is a nonzero vector.

124
00:29:31,984 --> 00:29:48,498
好的，你要做的是取向量 b；它是非零的，因此存在唯一一条垂直于它的直线。
Okay, so what you do is you take the vector b; it's nonzero, so therefore there's a unique line orthogonal to it.

125
00:29:48,498 --> 00:30:12,650
由于它非零，我们能找到一条正交直线，然后我们向该直线北侧取角度 theta/2，向南侧取 theta/2，这样我们就围绕这条正交直线得到一个扇形区域，夹角总共为 theta。我们沿这个方向旋转 theta。
Since it's nonzero, we can find an orthogonal line, and then we take angle theta over 2 to the north of it and theta over 2 to the south, so that we have a sector around this orthogonal line where the total angle here is theta. And we're going to rotate theta in this direction.

126
00:30:12,650 --> 00:30:22,326
这就是——我们给定了两个已知条件：在这个变换中给定了向量 b 和非零角 theta，我们要找不动点。
That's the—so we're given two things: we're given a vector b and a nonzero angle theta in this transformation, and we're trying to find the fixed point.

127
00:30:22,326 --> 00:30:33,152
所以我取垂直于b 的直线，围绕它取一个总角为 theta 的扇区，即在该线上方取一条成 theta/2 角的线，在下方取成theta/2 角的线。
So I take the line orthogonal to b, I take a sector around it where the total angle is theta, namely, I take this line of degree theta over 2 above this line and then theta over 2 below this line.

128
00:30:33,152 --> 00:30:47,786
好的，现在考虑向量 b 并在这个扇区中向外移动（射线间距越来越大）。由连续性，你最终会到达一个两射线间距等于 b 长度的位置：我们有一个平行于 b 的向量，从这里起始并终止于那里。
All right, now take this vector b and start moving up in this sector, which gets larger and larger and larger. And by continuity, you eventually come to a point where we have a vector parallel to b—let's see if I can even draw it—which starts here and ends there.

129
00:30:47,786 --> 00:31:00,224
它平行于 b。这看起来平行吗？足够接近了！在该扇区中存在唯一位置，使得平行于 b 的向量从这里连到这里，对吧？
That's parallel to b. Does that look parallel? Close enough! There's a unique point in this sector where a vector parallel to b goes from here to here, right?

130
00:31:00,224 --> 00:31:09,131
因为由于连续性该扇区逐渐张开，并且由垂直于该线的向量连接（因为它们平行于 b）。
Because this sector is by continuity getting larger, and eventually they are separated by—you're taking vectors perpendicular to this line because they're parallel to b.

131
00:31:09,131 --> 00:31:17,865
所以你从短向量开始，它变得越来越长，最终你会得到一个长度恰好为 |b| 的向量，停下！
So you start off with short vectors, and getting longer and longer and longer, and eventually you get to a vector of exact length b, and you stop!

132
00:31:17,865 --> 00:31:21,610
好的，断言是：这就是点 P，该点固定不动！
Okay, the claim is this is the point P: this point is fixed!

133
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:34,435
我们至少构造出了一个不动点。让我们看看为什么：变换是什么？变换是先旋转 theta 再平移 b。
It's at least one point that we've constructed that's fixed. Let's see why: what's the transformation? The transformation is rotate by theta and then translate by b.

134
00:31:34,435 --> 00:31:53,010
当我们把该点旋转 theta 时，我们转到了这个点，对吧？因为我们把它旋转了角度 theta。然后当我们平移 b 时，我们正好回到了这个点。
When we rotate this point by theta, we go to this point, correct? Because we've rotated it through an angle of theta. And then when we translate by b, we go right back to this point T_b.

135
00:31:53,010 --> 00:32:02,510
所以这就是我们的不动点！现在我断言：不动点仅此一个，不会再有其他不动点了，好吗？
So there's our fixed point! Now I claim that's it, that's it, no more fixed points, okay?

136
00:32:02,510 --> 00:32:25,920
因为一旦在平面上固定了一个点，平面的刚体运动就必须保持与该点距离固定的圆周上的点，因为现在它保持从 P 到 v 的距离，并且它还保持点 P 不动，对吧？
Because once I fix a point in the plane and I have a motion of a plane, it has to fix the points at a fixed distance from that point, because it preserves now the distance from P to v, and it also preserves the point P, right?

137
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:33,549
而在行列式为 1 的条件下唯一能发生的事情，就是绕圆周将你旋转一个角度 theta。
And the only thing that can happen if you have determinant 1 is it just rotates you around the circle by an angle of theta.

138
00:32:33,549 --> 00:32:43,454
所以我把最终证明留给大家：如果它还固定别的点，那么被固定的向量就太多了。
So I leave the final proof of that to you: if it fixed anything else, then there are too many vectors that are fixed.

139
00:32:43,454 --> 00:32:55,616
每个处于正距离的向量都必须被旋转一个确定的角度，因为该变换不是恒等变换，theta 和 b 都是非零的。
You know, each vector at positive distance has to be rotated by a positive angle, because this transformation is not the identity transformation, because both theta and b are nonzero.

140
00:32:55,616 --> 00:32:58,124
只要其中之一非零，它就不是恒等变换。
If either of them is nonzero, it's the non-identity transformation.

141
00:32:58,124 --> 00:33:11,449
所以总结来说，一旦你有了不动点 P，它保持与 P 的距离，并且它保持正交性。
So finish it by saying that once you have a fixed point P, it preserves the distance from P, and then it preserves orthogonality.

142
00:33:11,449 --> 00:33:25,060
因此一旦你知道它把向量映到哪里——假设你从以 P 为起点的一组正交向量出发，它将这组向量旋转某个角 theta，正如我们之前确定保原点变换的证明一样。
So once you know where it takes a vector—so you start with, say, an orthogonal set of vectors coming out of P, it rotates this through some angle theta, just like our previous proof that we identified the transformations that fix the origin.

143
00:33:25,060 --> 00:33:31,661
因此它必须把该向量映为与其正交且等长的向量，只有两种选择。
Therefore it has to take this vector to something of the same length which is orthogonal to this vector, so there are only two choices.

144
00:33:31,661 --> 00:33:36,095
然后你看哪一个的行列式为 1，结果必是一个旋转。
And then you see which one has determinant 1, and it turns out to be a rotation.

145
00:33:36,095 --> 00:33:46,342
书中会向大家展示，给定类似变换时如何找到那条逐点固定或作为整体固定的直线，我就不多讲了。
So the book will show you, if you're given a transformation like this, how you find the line that it fixes pointwise or that it fixes as a line, and I'll leave that.

146
00:33:46,342 --> 00:34:05,820
但这是很有趣的几何构造，证明了任何变换要么固定一个点，要么什么都不固定，要么有一条不变直线。好的，有了对单个元素的认识，我们现在回到作为整体的群。
But this is some amusing geometric construction to show that any transformation either fixes a point, or fixes nothing, or has a line that is stable. Okay, now with this knowledge of individual elements, we're going to go back to the group as a whole.

147
00:34:05,820 --> 00:34:14,944
单个元素性质都很好，这表明对 G 中的任意单个元素你都能从几何上理解它。
Individual elements are all very nice, and what this is saying that any one element in G you can sort of understand the geometry of it.

148
00:34:14,944 --> 00:34:25,974
当然，把 G 中的元素复合起来会变得相当复杂：如果你有一个固定点 P 的元素，又有另一个固定点 Q 的元素，你把它们复合起来，
Of course composing elements in G becomes quite complicated: if you have an element that fixes a point P and you have an element that fixes another point Q and you compose those, right,

149
00:34:25,974 --> 00:34:37,439
对吧，那会固定另一个依赖于 P 和 Q 的点，因为它属于这个子群。但具体是哪个点等等，就会变得相当复杂。
that's going to fix another point depending on P and Q, because it's going to be in this subgroup. But which point it is, etc., it gets quite complicated.

150
00:34:37,439 --> 00:34:45,200
所以我们现在要回过头来把群作为一个整体进行研究，首先我们将研究它的有限子群。
So we're going to go back to study now the group as a whole, and we're going to study first the finite subgroups of it.

151
00:34:52,560 --> 00:34:55,486
一个有限子群我将记作 Gamma。
Now a finite subgroup I'm going to call Gamma.

152
00:34:55,486 --> 00:35:22,644
运动群本身当然是一个无限群；事实上，如果我的子群中包含平移，它的阶就不是有限的，因为如果我一直做平移，就会越移越远，永远无法回到出发点。所以有限子群不能包含任何非平凡平移。
This is of course an infinite group; in fact, if I have a translation in my subgroup, it's not of finite order, because if I just keep doing a translation, I keep translating out and out and out and out and out, and I never get back to where I started. So this has no translations in it.

153
00:35:22,644 --> 00:35:36,360
任何有限子群都不包含平移：它当然可以包含绕某个点的旋转，也可以包含反射，因为我们在仅保原点的群的情形中已经见过，
Any finite subgroup contains no translations: it can certainly contain rotations around a point, and it can certainly contain reflections, because we've seen in the case of just the group fixing the origin,

154
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:50,975
你可以绕圆周旋转三分之一周，连转三次就回到了原点，所以那将是一个 3 阶元；或者反射给出有限阶元素。所以有限子群有各种可能性。
you could rotate a third of the way around the circle, and if you did that three times you'd be back to the origin, so that would be an element of order 3; or the reflections give you elements of finite order. So there are all kinds of possibilities for finite subgroups.

155
00:35:50,975 --> 00:36:09,649
第一个定理是——而且非常实用——任何有限子群 Gamma 在 R^2 中必固定一个公共点 P：即不仅每个元素固定某个点，
The first theorem is—and this is very useful—any finite Gamma fixes a point P in R^2: namely, not just each element fixes a point,

156
00:36:09,649 --> 00:36:24,170
而且该定理指出存在一个被群中所有元素共同固定的点，即对 Gamma 中的所有 gamma，都有 gamma(P) = P。
but the theorem is that there is a point that's fixed by every element in the group, i.e., gamma(P) is equal to P for all gamma in Gamma.

157
00:36:28,659 --> 00:36:34,960
这就是有限子群分类的关键，一旦我们证明了这一点，我们就能相当迅速地完成分类。
So that's the key to the classification of finite subgroups, and then we'll finish it rather quickly once we prove that.

158
00:36:34,960 --> 00:36:48,493
所以同样地，如果你断言——就像我断言这个复合变换固定某点一样——你必须能够指出是哪个点，必须给出该不动点P 的具体构造方法。
So again, if you claim that—just like I claimed that this composition fixed some point—you have to be able to show which point it is, you have to give a recipe for that point P that's fixed.

159
00:36:48,493 --> 00:37:34,224
我给大家一个抽象的构造法则：它是这样的。 设 s 为任意点、任意向量， 并考虑向量 gamma(s)，其中 gamma 属于有限群 Gamma。我们从某个向量 s 开始，把群作用在它上面：
So I'll give you an abstract recipe: it goes like this.   Let s be any point, any vector,   and consider the vectors gamma(s) where gamma is in this finite group Gamma. So we start with some vector s, and we start applying the group to it:

160
00:37:34,224 --> 00:37:56,685
得到一些新向量 gamma_1(s), gamma_2(s)等等，这在平面上定义了有限个向量的集合（可能含有重复——gamma 可能固定 s，我们不在乎）。这是平面 R^2 中的有限个向量，对吧？
we get some new vectors gamma_1(s), gamma_2(s), etc., and that defines a finite set of vectors in the plane, possibly with repeats—gamma might fix s, we don't really care. So this is a finite set of vectors in R^2, okay?

161
00:37:56,685 --> 00:38:05,440
现在这就是绝妙的想法：让 P 为这个集合的质心（重心）。
And now this is the brilliant idea: you let P be the center of mass of this set.

162
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:26,457
设 N 为该集合中元素的个数——比如 N 个向量（即使有重复也无所谓），因此 N 就是Gamma 的阶，我们不妨就这么设定。
So let N be the number of elements in this set—say N distinct vectors, or we'll even do it, say, N vectors possibly with repeats, we don't care, so N is the order of Gamma,

163
00:38:26,457 --> 00:38:46,990
令 P 为 1/N 乘以所有 gamma in Gamma 的 gamma(s) 的和。这里的和指的是向量求和，所以你把它们加起来，然后除以实数 N（乘以 1/N），其中 N 是向量的数量。
let's do it this way. And let P be 1/N times the sum over gamma in Gamma of gamma(s). So this sum means the vector sum, so you sum them up, and then you divide by the real number N (multiply by 1/N), where N is the number of vectors.

164
00:38:46,990 --> 00:38:59,448
这就像重心（barycenter）一样。如果你把四个这样的向量相加并除以4，你就会找到那里的中心，那就是 P。
So that's like a barycenter or something like that. If you added up four vectors like this and you divided by 4, you'd find the center there, that's P.

165
00:38:59,448 --> 00:39:10,090
好的，断言是 P 被固定：断言 P 是一个不动点！
Okay, the claim is P is fixed: the claim is that P is a fixed point!

166
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:40,960
那么，来看看当你把 G 中的任意元素 g 作用于 P 时会发生什么？g 可以是平移，也可以是线性映射。
Well, you see what happens when you apply g to P, an arbitrary element in G? Well, it could be a translation or it could be a linear map.

167
00:39:40,960 --> 00:40:06,660
记住，只需验证——断言是如果 g 属于一般运动群 G，那么 g(P)等于 1/N 乘以 g(gamma(s)) 的和。
So remember, it is enough to check—the claim is if g is in G (this is the general group), then g(P) is equal to 1/N times the summation of g(gamma(s)).

168
00:40:06,660 --> 00:40:19,374
你用 g 变换所有的点，把它们加起来，并取其平均值：对 G 中的任意 g（不仅是 Gamma）你得到的就是 g(P)。
So you translate all the points by g, and you sum them up, and you take their average: that's what you get for g(P) for any g in G, not just Gamma.

169
00:40:19,374 --> 00:40:30,224
验证这一点就足够了——记住，这个群是 R^2 与 O(2) 的半直积，所以只需对平移和旋转分别进行验证。
Well, it's enough to check this—remember, this group was R^2 semidirect O(2), so it's enough to check for translations and rotations.

170
00:40:30,224 --> 00:40:41,922
对旋转显然成立，因为 g 是线性映射，所以当你把它作用于前面带有常数因子的向量和时，常数提出，直接得到变换后的和。
It's clear for rotations because g is a linear map, so when you apply it to a sum of vectors with a constant in front of each, you just get the sum of the g's.

171
00:40:41,922 --> 00:40:57,533
而对于平移，你只需验证：如果平移所有点，你把 b 加了 N 次，然后再除以N，结果正好是对原向量加上了 b，这恰好等于把 g 作用在 P 上。
And for translation, well, you just have to check that if you translate all the points, you've added b N times to this, then you divide by N, so you've added b to this vector, which is exactly what you do if you apply g to P.

172
00:40:57,533 --> 00:41:07,405
所以如果你分别对平移和正交变换进行了验证，那么对它们的复合也同样成立：旋转成立因为是线性映射，
So if you check it separately for translations and for orthogonal transformations, then it's true for the composite too:

173
00:41:07,405 --> 00:41:33,458
平移成立因为除以了 N，N 个 b 求和再乘 1/N 就等于 b，你所用的正是这一点。好，现在将此应用于 Gamma 中的元素。
these because they're linear maps, and these because you've divided by N, so the summation of b N times 1/N is equal to b, that's what you're using. Well, now apply this to gamma in Gamma.

174
00:41:33,458 --> 00:41:50,240
若这样算，我们得到 gamma'(P)（不妨记作 gamma'）等于 1/N 乘以gamma' gamma(s) 对所有 gamma in Gamma 的求和。但这些元素不过是遍历群元素的另一种方式，对吧？
If you do that, we get gamma'(P) is—let's call it gamma'—1/N times the summation of gamma' gamma(s), summing over gamma in Gamma. But these elements are just another way of running through the group, right?

175
00:41:50,240 --> 00:41:58,500
如果我在有限群中有一组元素，并在左侧全部乘以群中的某个固定元素，我只是得到了群中元素的一个重新排列。
If I have a collection of elements in a finite group and I multiply them all on the left by one element in the group, I just get another reordering of the elements in the group.

176
00:41:58,500 --> 00:42:05,442
因此这个求和中的元素与原始求和中的元素完全相同，可能只是顺序不同。
So the elements in this sum are exactly the same as the elements in the original sum, perhaps in a different order.

177
00:42:05,442 --> 00:42:17,519
但向量加法是可交换的，我们不在乎按什么顺序相加，所以这与 1/N sum gamma(s) 完全相同，即等于 P！
But vector addition is commutative; we don't care what order we add them up, so this is the same thing as 1/N summation of gamma(s), which is P!

178
00:42:17,519 --> 00:42:36,915
只需重新排列求和中的各项，加之向量加法可交换。
Just rearrange the terms in the sum, and vector addition is commutative.

179
00:42:38,385 --> 00:42:48,268
现在大家明白为什么我们需要有限群来得到不动点了：如果对一般子群求和这毫无意义，因为我们不知道如何把无限多个向量相加。
Now you see why we needed a finite group to get a fixed point: this doesn't make any sense if you sum over a general subgroup, because we don't know how to add up an infinite number of vectors.

180
00:42:48,268 --> 00:42:56,441
但对于有限群，无论它有多大，我们都可以把这些向量加起来，除以向量的个数：这在平面上给出一个新向量，那就是不动点！
But for a finite group, no matter how large, we can add up those vectors, divide by the number of vectors: that gives us a new vector in the plane, and that's the fixed point!

181
00:42:56,441 --> 00:43:14,917
好的，现在我们知道保原点的子群：如果这个不动点就是原点（如果 P = 0），那么 Gamma 实际上就是我们所说的 O(2) 的子群。
Okay, now we know the subgroup fixing the origin: if this fixed point is the origin, if P is equal to 0, then Gamma is actually a subgroup of what we called O(2).

182
00:43:14,917 --> 00:43:39,038
一般情况下，Gamma 现在是其某个共轭群的子群：由于 Gamma 固定点 P，Gamma 实际上是 G 中固定点 P 的子群 G_P（满足 g(P) = P 的 g）的子群。
In general, Gamma is now a subgroup of a conjugate of that: so since Gamma fixes a point P, Gamma is actually a subgroup of the subgroup of G fixing P inside of G: G_P, where g(P) = P.

183
00:43:39,038 --> 00:43:51,819
并且我断言该子群恰好是如下的群：它是 G_0 用平移 T_P 进行的共轭：T_P G_0 T_P^{-1}。
And I claim that this group is exactly the following group: it's G_0 conjugated by T_P: T_P G_0 T_P^{-1}.

184
00:43:59,200 --> 00:44:12,898
我们来验证这个群中的元素是否固定 P：如果我们把 T_P^{-1} 作用在 P 上，它变到了 0；G_0 保持 0 不动；然后 T_P 将其平移回到 P。
Well, let's check that the elements in this group fix P. If we apply T_P^{-1} to P, it goes to 0; G_0 fixes 0; and then T_P translates it back to P.

185
00:44:12,898 --> 00:44:22,776
所以这些元素必然固定 P。反过来，如果你有一个固定 P 的元素，用 T_P^{-1} 共轭就会得到一个保持 0 不动的元素。
So these elements certainly fix P. And conversely, if you have an element that fixes P, then conjugating it by T_P^{-1} takes you to an element that fixes 0.

186
00:44:22,776 --> 00:44:26,509
因此 G_0 的这个共轭群正是 G_P。
So this conjugate of G_0 is exactly G_P.

187
00:44:26,509 --> 00:44:50,681
反过来，如果我们将 Gamma 共轭——这不会改变它作为有限群的抽象结构；记住，共轭是该群的一个自同构——那么 T_P^{-1} Gamma T_P 现在就是 G_0 的子群，不妨称其为 Gamma^*之类。
And conversely, if we then conjugate Gamma—which doesn't change its structure as a finite group; remember, conjugation is an automorphism of this group—so T_P^{-1} Gamma T_P is now a subgroup of G_0, call this maybe Gamma^* or something.

188
00:44:51,099 --> 00:44:59,097
这是同构于 Gamma 的有限群，而这就是群 O(2)。
So this is a finite group isomorphic to Gamma, and this is the group O(2).

189
00:44:59,097 --> 00:45:10,439
所以我们证明了：这个复杂的运动群中的有限子群，同构于相对简单的群 O(2) 的有限子群。
So what we've proved is that the finite subgroups of this complicated group are isomorphic to the finite subgroups of this rather simple group O(2).

190
00:45:10,439 --> 00:45:21,972
当我们尝试研究所谓的离散子群时这就不再成立了；但至少对于有限子群，转到整个运动群并没有带来任何额外的群论一般性；
That's not going to be true when we try to do what are called discrete subgroups of this motion group, but at least for finite subgroups we don't really gain any generality by going to the motion group;

191
00:45:21,972 --> 00:45:35,174
我们完全可以留在保持原点不动的子群内部，因为任意有限子群都固定某点，通过用把该点映到原点的平移进行共轭，我们就能把该子群移到保原点的子群中。
we might as well just stay inside of the subgroup that fixes the origin, because any finite subgroup fixes a point, and by conjugating by the translation that takes that point to the origin, we can move the subgroup into the subgroup fixing the origin.

192
00:45:35,174 --> 00:45:45,609
因此如果我们只对这些有限群的抽象代数结构感兴趣，我们完全可以归结为对 O(2) 的有限子群进行分类，好吗？
And so if we're only interested in the abstract structure of these finite groups, we might as well classify the finite subgroups of O(2), okay?

193
00:45:45,609 --> 00:45:52,730
所以这就是我现在要做的，以此作为本讲的结尾：我将告诉大家 O(2) 的所有有限子群是什么。
So now that's what I'm going to do, that's how I'm going to finish: I'm going to tell you what are all the finite subgroups of O(2).

194
00:45:58,570 --> 00:46:03,569
这其实只有两种可能性。
Well, there are really two possibilities.

195
00:46:09,370 --> 00:46:29,231
对 O(2) 中的有限子群 Gamma 进行分类。第一种情形：Gamma 包含在 SO(2) 中，即 Gamma 中的每个元素都是旋转。
So classify a finite Gamma in O(2). Now case 1: Gamma might be contained in SO(2), namely, everything in Gamma might be a rotation.

196
00:46:29,231 --> 00:46:45,620
第二种情形是 Gamma 与 SO(2) 的交集（我们记作 Gamma^+）在 Gamma 中的指数为 2，且是一个正规子群。
And case 2 is Gamma intersect SO(2)—let's call that Gamma^+—has index 2 in Gamma and is a normal subgroup.

197
00:46:47,550 --> 00:46:53,730
所以要么该群全由旋转构成，要么它与旋转群的交是一个指数为 2 的子群。
So either the group is contained in rotations, or its intersection with rotations is a subgroup of index 2.

198
00:46:53,730 --> 00:47:04,890
前者是 Gamma 中所有元素的行列式全为 +1 的情形；后者是 Gamma 中元素的行列式取值 +1 或 -1，
Well, this is the situation where the determinant of everything in Gamma is +1; and this is the situation where the determinant of everything in Gamma is either +1 or -1,

199
00:47:04,890 --> 00:47:16,365
且包含行列式为 -1 的元素，而 Gamma^+ 是行列式为 +1 的子群。因此我们得到从 Gamma 到{+1, -1} 的行列式同态。
and you have elements of determinant -1, and Gamma^+ is the subgroup where the determinant is +1. And so we get this homomorphism, the determinant, from Gamma to {+1, -1}.

200
00:47:16,365 --> 00:47:24,609
在第一种情形下它是平凡同态；在第二种情形下它是满同态，因此其核的指数为 2。
And in the first case it's the trivial homomorphism, and in the second case it's surjective, and so its kernel is of index 2.

201
00:47:24,609 --> 00:47:29,902
所以你在这类情形下得到一些群，在那类情形下得到另一些群。
So you get some groups in this case, and you get some groups in this case.

202
00:47:29,902 --> 00:47:49,950
我们先处理第一种情形：在情形一中，Gamma 中的每个元素都是绕某个角度 theta 的旋转，其中 0 <= theta < 2pi，对吧？
Let's do this case first: I claim in case 1, so therefore everything in Gamma is—so every gamma is some rotation through some angle theta, where 0 <= theta < 2pi, okay?

203
00:47:49,950 --> 00:48:22,510
现在如果我们想对其分类，我们要进行如下论证：设 theta 为 Gamma 中任意元素大于 0 的最小旋转角。当然你包含旋转角为 0 的恒等元，所以我们寻找最小的正旋转角。
Now if we want to classify it, we're going to do the following argument: let theta be the smallest angle of rotation for any element gamma in Gamma where theta is greater than 0. Of course you have the identity element that rotates through nothing, so we find the smallest angle of rotation.

204
00:48:22,510 --> 00:48:35,080
比如这是向量 e_1，这是 gamma(e_1)。旋转角只有有限个，所以必然存在一个最小角，对吧？
So this is, you know, the vector e_1, and this would be gamma(e_1). There are only a finite number of angles of rotation, so there's a smallest one, okay?

205
00:48:35,080 --> 00:49:17,026
那么断言是：这就是最小角， 而 Gamma 是由该元素生成的循环群，由这个元素生成； 并且如果 Gamma 的阶等于 n，这个角 theta 就等于 2pi/n，好吗？
Then the claim is that the element that—this is it then,   and Gamma is a cyclic group generated by this element;   and if the order of Gamma is equal to n, this angle theta is 2pi/n, okay?

206
00:49:17,026 --> 00:49:31,060
为了证明它是循环群，你只需说：假设我在群里还有别的旋转角，比如这里的 theta'，我需要证明的是theta' 是 theta 的某个整数倍。
Well, to prove it's a cyclic group, you just say, well, if I had something else in this—suppose I had some other angle of rotation, I don't know, here it is theta prime—and what I have to show is that theta prime is some multiple of theta.

207
00:49:31,060 --> 00:49:43,999
如果不是，我就会找到一个小于 theta' 的倍数，以及一个大于 theta' 的倍数，通过用该元素乘以 gamma 的这个倍数的逆，
Well, if it weren't, I'd get a multiple that was less than theta prime, I'd get a multiple that was bigger than theta prime, and by taking this element times this multiple of gamma inverse,

208
00:49:43,999 --> 00:49:57,279
我就会在群里找到一个旋转角比 theta 还小的非零旋转元素！这就像证明循环群的子群都是循环群一样；这其实就是伪装成角度的欧几里得辗转相除法（带余除法）。
I'd find an element that was smaller than theta which was an angle of rotation in the group! So it's just like proving that subgroups of a cyclic group are cyclic; it's really the Euclidean algorithm disguised as angles.

209
00:49:57,279 --> 00:50:01,664
这就证明了群中的任何元素都必须是 theta 的倍数。
So that proves that any element in the group has to be a multiple of theta.

210
00:50:01,664 --> 00:50:08,447
如果你希望该元素的阶为 n，你就必须恰好绕圆周旋转了 1/n 圈，这意味着旋转角必须是 2pi/n。
And if you want this element to have order n, you have to have rotated exactly 1/n around the circle, which means the angle is 2pi/n.

211
00:50:08,447 --> 00:50:18,788
请注意，任何这样的循环群都能作为有限群出现，因为我只要取这个角度，就得到了 SO(2) 中的一个 n 阶有限元；
And note that any such cyclic group can occur as a finite group, because I just take this angle, and that gives me an element of finite order n in SO(2);

212
00:50:18,788 --> 00:50:34,200
如果我取由其生成的循环群，就得到了一个 n 阶有限循环群。特别地，这里的每个子群都是循环群，且所有阶数都会出现。
and if I take the cyclic group generated by this, I get a finite cyclic group of order n. In particular, every subgroup here is cyclic, and all orders occur.

213
00:50:38,380 --> 00:50:46,213
所以这是处理循环群的绝佳方式：所有循环群都是 SO(2) 的子群。
So that's a nice way of doing cyclic groups: all cyclic groups are subgroups of SO(2).

214
00:50:46,213 --> 00:50:57,055
好的，让我们在这个情形下迅速收尾：我们知道这个群是循环群，因为它是 SO(2) 的有限子群。
Okay, here, let's finish this quickly in this case: we know that this group is cyclic because it's a finite subgroup of SO(2).

215
00:50:57,055 --> 00:51:18,239
所以子群 Gamma^+ 是某个 n 阶循环群，并且它在 Gamma 中的指数为 2，从而 Gamma 的阶为 2n。它包含一个——不妨把这个群记作 C_n，一个指数为 2 的循环子群。
So this group Gamma^+ is cyclic of some order n, and it has index 2 in Gamma, so that Gamma has order 2n. And it contains in it—let me call this group C_n, a cyclic group of index 2.

216
00:51:18,239 --> 00:51:24,500
现在它还必须包含一个反射，因为我们说过某个元素上的行列式为 -1。
Now it also has to contain a reflection, because we said the determinant was -1 on some element.

217
00:51:24,500 --> 00:51:47,376
因此在 Gamma 中取一个不属于该循环子群的元素：设其为关于直线 L 的反射，不妨记为 r。那么 r^2 等于1；在这个循环子群上，我们知道 r h r^{-1} = h^{-1}，对吧？
So take an element in Gamma which is not in this cyclic group: call that reflection across the line L, and call that maybe r. Then r^2 is equal to 1; and on this cyclic group, we know that r h r^{-1} is equal to h^{-1}, right?

218
00:51:47,376 --> 00:51:54,152
因为这对 SO(2) 中的任意元素都成立，特别地对该循环子群中的元素也成立。
Because that was true for an arbitrary element in SO(2), in particular for the elements in the cyclic group.

219
00:51:54,152 --> 00:52:14,830
所以我们看到在指数为 2 的情形下，Gamma 由两个元素生成：由一个旋转角为 2pi/n 的 n 阶旋转生成，以及由一个 2 阶反射 r 生成（满足 r^2 = 1）；
So we see that in the case where this group has index 2, Gamma is generated by two elements: it's generated by a rotation through an angle 2pi/n which has order n, and then it's generated by a reflection r which has order 2,

220
00:52:14,830 --> 00:52:28,634
旋转子群是正规子群，用 r 进行共轭时会对该子群中的每个元素给出求逆操作，因为在一般的 O(2) 中也是如此。
and r^2 = 1, and this is a normal subgroup, and when you conjugate by r you get inversion on this subgroup for every element, because that was true in the general O(2).

221
00:52:28,634 --> 00:52:35,437
并且这些群被称为二面体群，阶数为 2n。
And these groups are called dihedral groups of order 2n.

222
00:52:35,437 --> 00:52:46,307
当 n >= 3 时，它们是非交换群，因为在 H 内并非每个元素都等于其逆元。
And once n >= 3, they're non-abelian, because not every element is equal to its inverse inside of H.

223
00:52:46,307 --> 00:52:55,844
我们在之前见过的二面体群的典型例子，就是 3 个字母上的对称群 S_3 同构于 6 阶二面体群。
And a typical example of a dihedral group that we've seen before is the symmetric group on 3 letters is isomorphic to the dihedral group of order 6.

224
00:52:55,844 --> 00:53:03,494
这个群我记作 D_{2n}；书上称其为 D_n，但我喜欢追踪群的阶数。
This group I will call D_{2n}; the book calls it D_n, but I like to keep track of the order.

225
00:53:03,494 --> 00:53:18,343
所以这里是 n 阶循环群，所有的循环群都会出现；而在另一边我们得到 2n 阶二面体群，所有的 2n 阶二面体群都会出现。这些就是 G_0（即 O(2)）内部的全部有限群。
So here this is the cyclic group of order n, and all cyclic groups occur; here we get the dihedral group of order 2n, and all dihedral groups of order 2n occur. And those are the finite groups inside of G_0, inside of O(2).

226
00:53:18,343 --> 00:53:26,912
特别地，运动群 G 的任何有限子群要么同构于循环群，要么同构于二面体群！
And in particular, any finite subgroup of G is isomorphic either to a cyclic group or a dihedral group!

227
00:53:26,912 --> 00:53:37,034
现在这仅仅是个开始，下一步我们不是要对运动群的有限子群进行分类，而是要分类所谓的离散子群。
Now this is just the beginning, the next thing we're going to do is not classify the finite groups of this motion group, but what are called the discrete groups.

228
00:53:37,034 --> 00:53:39,672
那正是我们深入探索美妙对称性研究的切入点。
And that's where we get into the beautiful study of symmetry.

229
00:53:39,672 --> 00:53:48,029
所以请务必把这些内容牢记在心，因为有限子群其实只是离散群的一个子集，但离散群还将包含平移之类的变换。
So make sure you have this down in your head, because finite subgroups turn out to be a subset of the discrete groups, but the discrete groups are going to have things like translations in them.

230
00:53:48,029 --> 00:53:56,535
这就是我们周五要讲的内容，好的。
So that's what we're heading for on Friday, okay?
